{
  "id": "KP320",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Surgical knee repair (knee arthroscopy)",
  "description": "A surgical knee repair is an outpatient procedure where your surgeon repairs damaged cartilage, ligaments, tendons, or other structures in your knee using arthroscopic or open surgical techniques. Knee injuries like meniscal tears, ligament tears, or cartilage damage can cause pain and instability. Your surgeon will assess your knee and perform the necessary repairs. The procedure takes 1-2 hours, and you may go home the same day or stay overnight. You'll use crutches and wear a brace for several weeks while you heal. Physical therapy begins immediately and is crucial for success. You'll have specific activity restrictions during healing to protect your repair. Most patients return to their desired activities with proper rehabilitation.",
